      "low": {
        "title": "Low-Scoring Orchard",
        "narrative": "This orchard is materially below the regional average. The main weaknesses are irrigation (3/10) and management (4/10). The pest component is also weak at 4/10, while climate is relatively neutral at 6/10, but not strong enough to offset the weaker drivers.",
        "bankView": "This is a weak lead.\nIt should not be treated as a fast-approval case.\n\nWhat the Bank should focus on at underwriting stage:\n\n• Request a more detailed business plan, especially around operational stability\n• Verify why irrigation performance is weak and how this may affect output and income generation\n• Apply more conservative cash flow assumptions\n• Assess whether this is a temporary setback or a structural weakness",
        "monitoringTab": "This case should be classified as Red / Attention Needed.\n\nWhat the Bank should monitor:\n\n• Whether the score continues to decline in the coming months\n• Whether irrigation and management improve or remain weak\n• Whether the gap versus the regional average narrows or widens\n\nWhat actions the Bank can take on an already disbursed loan:\n\n• Move the case into enhanced monitoring\n• Review the account more frequently\n• Request updated operational and performance information\n• If the score declines further, move it to a formal watchlist\n• Treat it as a priority review case for the relationship manager"
      },
      "mid": {
        "title": "Mid-Scoring Orchard",
        "narrative": "The orchard is close to the regional average, but one to two weaker components are limiting its overall score. Climate is strong at 8/10, and pests are moderate at 6/10, but management (5/10) and irrigation (6/10) keep the orchard from moving into a stronger segment.",
        "bankView": "<p>This is a <strong>possible lead</strong>, but one that requires selective review.</p><p><strong>What the Bank should focus on at underwriting stage:</strong></p><ul><li>Pay particular attention to the <strong>management weakness</strong>, as it is the main limiting factor</li><li>Request a <strong>clearer explanation in the business plan</strong> of what will support stable performance in the coming seasons</li><li>Test whether the revenue assumptions are realistic</li><li>Approval should be considered only after <strong>additional review</strong></li></ul>",
        "monitoringTab": "<p><strong>What the Bank should monitor:</strong></p><ul><li>Whether the management component improves or remains the main weak point</li><li>Whether the orchard moves closer to the regional average or remains below it</li><li>Whether the current positive trend holds or starts to reverse</li></ul><p><strong>What actions the Bank can take on an already disbursed loan:</strong></p><ul><li>Put the account on a regular review cycle</li><li>Monitor whether it starts moving into the low-score segment</li><li>If the trend turns negative over the next 1–2 months, move it into a higher-priority monitoring group</li><li>If both the score and weakest driver improve, keep it under standard monitoring</li></ul>"
      },
      "high": {
        "title": "High-Scoring Orchard",
        "narrative": "This orchard is clearly above the regional average. Its strongest areas are management (9/10), irrigation (8/10), and pests (8/10). Climate is also strong at 9/10. The high score is not driven by a single factor — the orchard is strong across the full profile.",
        "bankView": "This is a good lead.\nIt is a stronger candidate both for new lending and for faster review.\n\nWhat the Bank should focus on at underwriting stage:\n\n• Confirm that the strong performance is stable and not one-off\n• Use the business plan discussion to assess growth potential, not only downside protection\n• This can be considered for faster review, given the high score and positive gap versus the regional average",
        "monitoringTab": "What the Bank should monitor:\n\n• Whether the high score is sustained over time\n• Whether the weakest criterion starts to deteriorate\n• Whether the orchard remains above the regional average or begins to converge downward\n\nWhat actions the Bank can take on an already disbursed loan:\n\n• Keep the account under standard monitoring\n• Use it as an example of a healthy portfolio case\n• If the trend remains stable, it may qualify for low-touch monitoring\n• If one of the components starts weakening, move it early into Yellow / Review"
      }
